Contributing Guidelines
All contributions, bug reports, bug fixes, documentation improvements, enhancements, and ideas are welcome.

How to Contribute
Fork the Repository: Create a copy of this repository in your GitHub account.
Clone the Repository: Download your fork to your local computer.
Create a Branch: Create a new branch for your changes.
Make Changes: Improve the code, fix bugs, update documentation, or suggest enhancements.
Test Your Changes: Ensure that your changes work correctly.
Commit Changes: Write a clear and meaningful commit message.
Submit a Pull Request: Send your changes for review.
Reporting Bugs
Clearly describe the problem.
Provide steps to reproduce the issue.
Include the expected and actual results.
Attach screenshots or error messages when applicable.
Suggesting Enhancements
Suggestions and new ideas are welcome. Please explain the proposed improvement and how it could benefit the project.

Documentation Improvements
You can contribute by correcting spelling mistakes, improving explanations, updating the README, or adding useful examples.

Code of Conduct
All contributors are expected to communicate respectfully and follow the guidelines in CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md.

Thank You
Thank you for your interest in contributing to this project. Every contribution, whether small or large, is appreciated
